<aura:documentation>
	<aura:description>
    
How they all work together in the life cycle:Initialization: 
Salesforce loads the SearchBar.cmp.DOM Insertion (Renderer): 
The framework draws the HTML. As soon as it finishes, SearchBarRenderer.js triggers 
afterRender(), which finds the input box and places the blinking typing cursor inside it.
User Action (Controller): The user types a word and clicks the button. 
This triggers handleSearchClick inside SearchBarController.js.Processing (Helper): 
The controller calls helper.cleanAndFormatQuery(). The helper sanitizes the text and 
returns it. The controller then updates the screen with the clean text.

    
    
    </aura:description>
	<aura:example name="ExampleName" ref="exampleComponentName" label="Label">
		Example Description
	</aura:example>
</aura:documentation>